<title>MEXICO: Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rate on Mexican government 728-day development bonds, or Bondes, rose 0.32 percentage points to 1.39 percent above the 28-day Cetes rate in Tuesday's primary auction, dealers estimated.</p>
<p>The 728-day Bondes were assigned at 97.81034 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the two-year Bondes was 2.16 billion pesos, compared with the 500 million offered by Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>The rate on the 364-day Bondes rose 0.06 percentage points to 1.25 percent above the 28-day Cetes rate, at an assigned price of 98.88899 pesos.</p>
<p>There were 500 million pesos assigned for the 364-day Bondes compared with 2.790 billion pesos worth demanded.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
